<ul>
<li>The <code>project_id</code> for a Neon project is found on the <strong>Settings</strong> page in the Neon Console, or you can find it by listing the projects for your Neon account using the Neon API.</li>
<li>The <code>parent_id</code> can be obtained by listing the branches for your project. See <a class="" href="#list-branches-with-the-api">List branches</a>. The <code>&lt;parent_id&gt;</code> is the <code>id</code> of the branch you are branching from. A branch <code>id</code> has a <code>br-</code> prefix. You can branch from your Neon project&#x27;s default branch or a previously created branch.</li>
</ul>
<p>The response body includes information about the branch, the branch&#x27;s compute, and the <code>create_branch</code> and <code>start_compute</code> operations that were initiated.</p>
